
# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# - why this change
# - side effects or prerequisites
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENGLISH ONLY. type, scope, subject, body and footer.
# Docs and code comments stay in Chinese; commit messages do not.
#
# subject   imperative, present tense, lower case, no trailing period,
#           72 chars max. No space before the colon.
#           Proper nouns keep their case: "add Discord account binding".
#           Say what you did, not which files you touched -- git has those.
#
# body      bullet points. Each one answers WHY, not WHAT.
#           If future-you would ask "why was it done this way", write it.
#
# footer    BREAKING CHANGE: <what broke>   also add ! after the type
#           Refs: #42
#
# type      feat      a capability users can see
#           fix       wrong behaviour corrected
#           refactor  internal change, behaviour unchanged
#           perf      performance
#           docs      documentation only
#           test      tests only
#           build     build, dependencies, Dockerfile
#           ci        workflows and CI config
#           chore     none of the above. Reaching for it often means
#                     the change was not classified properly
#           revert    revert
#
# scope     identity ledger outbox notify redeem activity
#           domain core http ws grpc cron storage
#           contracts migrations config e2e docs lint deps ci structure
#           Leave it out when the change spans several layers.
#
# One commit, one thing. If the subject needs "and", split it.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
